# Build-time map: EESSI software subdirectory -> EasyBuild optarch for RISC-V
#
# Runtime CPU selection uses eessi_archdetect.sh + eessi_arch_riscv.spec.
# This file is only for compile flags at build time. Detection ISA tokens and
# map flags are intentionally not always identical (see vendor notes below).
#
# Sole production consumer: EESSI-extend (EESSI-extend-easybuild.eb) parses
# this map in Lua and sets EASYBUILD_OPTARCH when EESSI_SOFTWARE_SUBDIR is
# riscv64/* and optarch is not already set (same pattern as CUDA/AMD compute
# capabilities). If the subdir has no map entry, EESSI-extend warns and leaves
# optarch unset (fall through) rather than failing module load — site installs
# may override. Map format checks live in tests/riscv_optarch/ (test-only).
#
# Format: <software_subdir><TAB_OR_SPACES><optarch>
#   - GENERIC means EasyBuild's RISC-V generic flags for each compiler
#     (GCC/Clang/LLVM: -march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d)
#   - otherwise EasyBuild multi-compiler syntax:
#       GCC:<flags>;Clang:<flags>;LLVM:<flags>
#     see https://docs.easybuild.io/controlling-compiler-optimization-flags/
#   - Trailing # comments on data lines are stripped by the Lua parser.
#
# Notes:
# - Path names may use profile labels (rva20u64, ...). -march must use explicit
#   rv64* ISA strings for toolchains that do not yet accept profile names as
#   -march (e.g. Ubuntu 24.04 gcc-riscv64 13.x / clang 18).
# - Omit -mtune=generic: unknown to some RISC-V GCC builds.
# - Omit S-mode / privileged extensions from -march (sscofpmf, sstc, sv*, ...):
#   they may appear in archdetect specs for matching but are not needed for
#   userspace codegen and break older Clang.
# - No SpacemiT -mtune/-mcpu name upstream yet: X60 entries are -march only.
# - map⊆spec (tests/riscv_optarch): every -march userspace token must be in the
#   matching archdetect spec. GENERIC and -mcpu-only rows are skipped — there
#   is no explicit -march to ⊆-check; the named -mcpu defines the ISA surface.
# - Spec lines must not use parentheses in trailing comments.

riscv64/generic			GENERIC
riscv64/rva20u64		GCC:-march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d;Clang:-march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d;LLVM:-march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d
riscv64/rva22u64		GCC:-march=rv64gc_zba_zbb_zbs_zfhmin_zicbom_zicbop_zicboz -mabi=lp64d;Clang:-march=rv64gc_zba_zbb_zbs_zfhmin_zicbom_zicbop_zicboz -mabi=lp64d;LLVM:-march=rv64gc_zba_zbb_zbs_zfhmin_zicbom_zicbop_zicboz -mabi=lp64d
riscv64/rva23u64		GCC:-march=rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs_zfhmin -mabi=lp64d;Clang:-march=rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs_zfhmin -mabi=lp64d;LLVM:-march=rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs_zfhmin -mabi=lp64d

# p550: userspace -march is a subset of measured cpuinfo (sscofpmf kept in the
# archdetect spec only). GCC gets -mtune=sifive-7-series; Clang/LLVM have no
# equivalent tune name here, so -march alone.
riscv64/sifive/p550		GCC:-march=rv64gc_zba_zbb -mtune=sifive-7-series -mabi=lp64d;Clang:-march=rv64gc_zba_zbb -mabi=lp64d;LLVM:-march=rv64gc_zba_zbb -mabi=lp64d

# u74-mc: archdetect keeps the full measured VisionFive /proc/cpuinfo tokens
# (zca/zcd/…). Do not freeze that host ISA as -march — it is kernel/board
# advertisement, not a stable EESSI compile contract, and GCC 14.3 (EESSI
# stack) accepts -mcpu=sifive-u74 which sets both ISA and U74 scheduling.
# Same -mcpu for GCC/Clang/LLVM. map⊆spec skips this row (no -march).
riscv64/sifive/u74-mc		GCC:-mcpu=sifive-u74 -mabi=lp64d;Clang:-mcpu=sifive-u74 -mabi=lp64d;LLVM:-mcpu=sifive-u74 -mabi=lp64d

# SpacemiT X60 is marketed RVA22 but is not a clean full RVA22U64 host (e.g.
# Zicclsm gap). Neither Banana Pi F3 fixture matches the rva22u64
# floor: Armbian lacks bitmanip/zfhmin; k6.6 advertises bitmanip/zfh* but not
# zicbop. Vendor paths exist so those boards get usable trees instead of
# falling through to a profile they cannot satisfy. -march is a frozen
# userspace subset of each kernel's measured isa (S-mode stripped); no -mtune.
riscv64/spacemit/x60		GCC:-march=rv64imafdcv_zicbom_zicboz_zicbop_zihintpause -mabi=lp64d;Clang:-march=rv64imafdcv_zicbom_zicboz_zicbop_zihintpause -mabi=lp64d;LLVM:-march=rv64imafdcv_zicbom_zicboz_zicbop_zihintpause -mabi=lp64d
riscv64/spacemit/x60-k6.6	GCC:-march=rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs_zfh_zfhmin_zicbom_zicboz_zihintpause -mabi=lp64d;Clang:-march=rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs_zfh_zfhmin_zicbom_zicboz_zihintpause -mabi=lp64d;LLVM:-march=rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs_zfh_zfhmin_zicbom_zicboz_zihintpause -mabi=lp64d
